  "description": "SAQWAK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H58 Dy4 N36 O5,C60 H58 Dy4 N36 O5,50(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy5 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.664-5.282 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.54-178.63°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(L1-2H)2(L1-H)2(N3)4(O)]·14H2O (crystal data: C60H58Dy4N36O5·25H2O).",
